/target

# Cargo.lock is COMMITTED on purpose, and must stay that way.
#
# The delegate key is BLAKE3 over the delegate WASM, so the exact dependency
# versions are part of the key. While this file was ignored, two checkouts of
# the same commit resolved differently (measured: 1699 differing lines) and
# produced different delegate keys -- meaning a stray `cargo update` could
# silently move every user's stored ghostkeys to a namespace nothing would
# ever look in. See ghostkeys#9 and scripts/build-delegate.sh.

# Secrets / credentials
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
secrets/

# Agent worktrees live here (.claude/worktrees/<name>), and committing one
# adds it as an embedded git repo rather than files. Easy to do by accident
# with `git add -A`.
.claude/
